## Runtime Usage

### Command-Line Interface (CLI)

Basic batch processing with all optimizations:
```bash
scantailor-cli --output-project=out.ScanTailor input/*.tif output/
```

Verbose mode shows processing details:
```bash
scantailor-cli --verbose --output-project=out.ScanTailor input/*.tif output/
```

**Print performance statistics after processing:**
```bash
scantailor-cli --print-stats --output-project=out.ScanTailor input/*.tif output/
# or use short form:
scantailor-cli -ps --output-project=out.ScanTailor input/*.tif output/
```

This prints a detailed performance report showing:
- Total processing time and pages per minute
- Per-operation timing (grayscale, morphology, SEDM, dewarping, etc.)
- Speedup comparison: SIMD vs CPU, GPU vs CPU
- Best backend for each operation
- Throughput in megapixels per second

Example output:
```
================================================================================
                    PERFORMANCE STATISTICS REPORT
================================================================================

Session Summary:
  Pages processed:    100
  Total time:         7.23 sec
  Avg time per page:  72.3 ms
  Pages per minute:   830.6

Detailed Operation Statistics:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Operation            Backend      Calls   Total(ms)     Avg(ms)     Min(ms)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
grayscale            SIMD           100       312.45        3.12        2.98
morphology           SIMD           200       845.32        4.23        3.89
dewarping            CPU            100      2345.67       23.46       21.34

Speedup Comparison (vs CPU baseline):
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Operation            SIMD Speedup   GPU Speedup    Best Backend
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
grayscale            4.2x           -              SIMD
morphology           3.1x           -              SIMD
================================================================================
```

### GUI Application

Launch normally - optimizations are automatic:
```bash
scantailor-universal
```

### Verifying GPU Acceleration

The application automatically uses GPU when available. To verify:

1. **Check CUDA availability** in your program:
```cpp
#include "gpu/CUDAUtils.h"

if (imageproc::gpu::initCUDA()) {
    auto info = imageproc::gpu::getCUDADeviceInfo();
    printf("GPU: %s (Compute %d.%d)\n",
           info.deviceName, info.major, info.minor);
    printf("Memory: %zu MB\n", info.totalMemory / (1024*1024));
} else {
    printf("CUDA not available: %s\n",
           imageproc::gpu::getLastCUDAError());
}
```

2. **Monitor GPU usage** during processing:
```bash
# In a separate terminal
watch -n 0.5 nvidia-smi
```

